<title>AUSTRALIA: Labour move halts New Caledonia nickel exports - SLN.</title>
<headline>Labour move halts New Caledonia nickel exports - SLN.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nickel exports from New Caledonia have been halted due to an industrial action, nickel producer Ste Metallurgique Le Nickel (SLN) said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;All exports have been halted,&quot; Jean Mouradian, general manager of SLN told Reuters.</p>
<p>Mouradian said smelting at SLN had not been affected by the action and that metal would be stockpiled for later shipment.</p>
<p>He said there was no need at this stage to declare force majeure on sales to customers.</p>
<p>The smelter produces about 4,500 tonnes of nickel a month, he said.</p>
</text>
